  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c7fa63be-87a6-4c5c-99c8-24e1cd3e41b6",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1152,
        -352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 708,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## 🧩 GHL Business Custom Field Creator – Sheet-Driven Setup\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow reads a list of custom fields you want on GoHighLevel's Business object from a Google Sheet, then creates only the ones still marked as pending. It loops through each row, skips anything not flagged `UNDONE`, and calls the GHL API to create the field. Once a field is created (or the call fails), the sheet is updated with the result — either the new field ID with a `Done` status, or an `Error` flag — so you always know where things stand. A global error trigger posts to Slack if anything in the run breaks.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Add your Google Sheets, GHL, and Slack credentials, then swap in your Sheet ID, GHL location ID, and parent field ID across the relevant nodes.\n2. In your sheet, list each field with a `key`, `Field Name`, `Suggested Field Type`, and a `Status` column set to `UNDONE` for anything you want created.\n3. Set your Slack channel ID on the alert node, then run the workflow manually and check the sheet for results."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
